/**
 * @defgroup ZcalGeo ZcalGeo — Zero-Degree Calorimeter Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Zero-Degree Calorimeter (ZDC)
 *
 * @details
 * The ZDC (detector tag **ZCAL**) is a quartz-scintillator-sampling calorimeter placed
 * at very large pseudorapidity (η > 6) to detect forward spectator neutrons from
 * nuclear collisions.  Two identical modules are placed symmetrically at z = ±1767.66 cm
 * from the interaction point, beyond the DX dipole magnets where neutral particles
 * separate from the beams.
 *
 * ### Physics role
 * - **Centrality determination** — the spectator neutron multiplicity is anticorrelated
 *   with the collision centrality in Au+Au and other heavy-ion collisions.
 * - **Luminosity monitoring** — coincidence of the east and west ZDC signals provides
 *   a minimum-bias trigger that is independent of detector acceptance.
 *
 * ### Detector structure
 * The sensitive calorimeter element (QCAL) is a 10 cm × 10 cm × 130 cm lead block
 * divided into 260 equal longitudinal slices (QDIV).  Each slice contains a 1 mm-thick
 * polystyrene scintillator layer (QSCI) acting as a sampling medium.  The geometry
 * also includes the beam-line hardware in that region:
 * - **PIPH** — large-diameter iron beam pipe (r_out = 20.96 cm, half-length = 133.35 cm)
 *   enclosing a vacuum bore (PVAH)
 * - **PLAT** — iron end plate at the downstream end of PIPH, with two circular holes
 *   (PLVA) for the diverging beam pipes
 * - **PIPJ** — the two final beam pipes (r_out = 6.35 cm), angled at ±1.074° in y,
 *   each containing a vacuum bore (PVAJ)
 *
 * Tight transport thresholds (CUTGAM = 0.5 MeV, CUTELE = 0.15 MeV) are applied within
 * QCAL and QSCI to correctly simulate the electromagnetic shower in the narrow
 * sampling layers.
 *
 * ### Placement
 * The west module is placed at z = +1767.66 cm in the WestRefSys reference frame;
 * the east module is placed at z = −1767.66 cm in EastRefSys with a 180° rotation
 * about z to invert the beam direction.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @file ZcalGeo.xml
 * @brief Module ZCALGEO — zero-degree calorimeter geometry (Christie, 1997).
 *
 * Defines structure **CALP** containing all geometry parameters:
 * - Mother tube: DROutR = 30 cm, DRdz = 250 cm
 * - Beam-pipe geometry: PHLeng, PHInnR, PHOutR, Pltdz, PltOutR, HOutR
 * - Final beam pipes: PJInnR = 6.07 cm, PJOutR = 6.35 cm, PJLeng = 91.5 cm
 * - Calorimeter: QCdx = QCdy = 5 cm, QCdz = 65 cm, SCdz = 0.05 cm, Sdiv = 260
 *
 * Volumes:
 * - ZCAL — Air mother tube placed at ±1767.66 cm
 * - QCAL — Lead box with tight transport cuts
 * - QDIV — division of QCAL into 260 layers
 * - QSCI — polystyrene scintillator slice (sensitive, eloss hit)
 * - PIPH/PVAH — large beam pipe and vacuum
 * - PLAT/PLVA — end plate and beam holes
 * - PIPJ/PVAJ — diverging final beam pipes and vacuum
 */

/**
 * @file ZcalConfig.xml
 * @brief Setup registry for detector ZCAL.
 *
 * | Setup | on/off | Notes |
 * |---|---|---|
 * | ZCALof | off | no ZDC |
 * | ZCALon | on  | both east and west modules |
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
